 :question
 {:id :task-state-preference-policy
  :text "How should deterministic task-state channels affect META choice, and what should happen to kinds without an authoritative value?"
  :options
  [{:id :categorical-support-filter-and-ranked-preferences
    :recommended true
    :rule "Keep explicit automated infeasibility as a support exclusion. Compare admitted candidates by separately declared categorical/ordinal preferences for current centrality and Tornhill proxy states; exclude only the missing channel from that candidate's comparison and require at least one common preferred channel against the nearest alternative."
    :why "This preserves feasibility as admission, avoids inventing observation noise, and never treats missing E/T/A measurements as zero."}
   {:id :finite-observation-noise-gaussian
    :recommended false
    :rule "Declare a strictly positive observation variance and numeric preference mean/weight for each normalized task-state channel, then use the existing Gaussian EFE port; candidates missing a declared channel are typed exclusions from that comparison."
    :why "This reuses the current evaluator but requires new numeric noise, direction, and relative-weight authority that no source currently supplies."}
   {:id :receipt-only-until-terminal-model-learned
    :recommended false
    :rule "Retain centrality, feasibility, and Tornhill only as reason-bearing receipt fields; do not let them affect G until registered evidence supports the existing terminal/resource channels."
    :why "This adds no new preference assumptions, but leaves the current field nondiscriminating."}]}

